Uses
They grow into rosettes of edible cress foliage that resemble dandelion leaves. Barbarea verna, known as upland cress, early winter cress, American cress, Belle Isle cress and scurvy grass, is used to add a spicy taste to salads and mixed leaf greens for cooking.{{Additional citation needed|date=August 2021}}

Chemical compounds
Winter cress contains different glucosinolates, flavonoids, and saponins.
